<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador's monetary base up 1.34 pct in week.</title>
<headline>Ecuador's monetary base up 1.34 pct in week.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's monetary base rose 1.34 percent to 2.72 billion sucres in the week to Sept 20, the Central Bank said Monday.</p>
<p>The bank did not explain the reasons for the increase.</p>
<p>In the previous week, monetary base fell 0.52 percent.</p>
<p>The monetary base ended 1995 at 2.41 billion sucres.</p>
<p>--Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, (5932) 258433</p>
